in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts, waiting 0.5s and then 1s between them. I ran it against a local HTTP server and it behaved as intended:\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 straight away | data returned | 1 |\n| 503, 503, then 200 | data returned | 3 |\n| 503 every time | `HTTPError 503` raised | 3 |\n| 500 | `HTTPError 500` raised | 1 (no retry) |\n\n- **Only 503 retries.** Any other error, and any 503 after the third attempt, is raised to the caller as before.\n- **New constructor argument:** I added `backoff=0.5` so the wait can be shortened (the test used 0.01s). The cap of 3 attempts is set by `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3` on the class.\n- **Not covered:** timeouts and connection errors still fail straight away without a retry.\n- **No tests in the repo:** I added none, so the table above is the only check run.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 105123, "requests_cache_write": 73095, "requests_cost_usd": 0.4198676, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1666, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial21", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 101, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:51:00.639631+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 19.95, "t_checker_s": 2.386, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1678, "tokens_cache_read": 105123, "tokens_cache_write": 73095, "tokens_fresh": 1